DERIVATIVE WORK (2026) — APLINKS server
---------------------------------------

Copyright (C) 2026  Jean-François Albouy
Located in:  modernized/aplinks/

This is a derivative of N.Kon's APLINKS 1.03 server (APLINKS.C). Changes:
  - ported from MS-DOS <dos.h> to ISO C (C99, plus a C17 variant) with a
    #ifdef _WIN32 / POSIX platform layer (builds on Windows, Linux, macOS);
  - added 128K/512K disk modes, a "disk folder" model, file-timestamp
    preservation, runtime serial options, verbose logging, free-space and
    session-history reporting.
The on-wire protocol and the virtual-disk logic are byte-for-byte unchanged
from N.Kon's original. All original copyright notices are preserved in the
source and in the produced binaries.

APLINKS 1.07 (APLINKS107.C -> aplinks32_107.exe, same folder) is a further
derivative of the 1.06 above, kept as a SEPARATE source: APLINKS.C 1.06 and its
binaries are left untouched as the reference. It adds a 256K disk mode, one
protocol addition (a mode query 'Q', which older servers ignore and which the
1999 driver never sends), and guards against out-of-disk sectors and broken FAT
chains. See modernized/aplinks/README-1.07.md.


DERIVATIVE WORK (2026) — PLINKC driver
--------------------------------------

Copyright (C) 2026  Jean-François Albouy
Located in:  modernized/plinkc/

This is a derivative of PLINKC 1.62 by Daisuke Mizobata (itself based on
PLINK.SYS 1.04 by N.Kon), made from the author's source PLINKC.asm preserved
in original/PLINKC-1.62-1999/. Changes, all to be assembled with xasm2026-4:
  - system constants taken from pce500.inc (generated include file);
  - uninstallation by CALL &BF000 "-U", and detailed "already installed"
    messages;
  - INIT "L:?" (driver state), INIT "L:H" (help), unknown options reported;
  - a 256K disk mode and the mode query 'Q' answered by APLINKS 1.07.
The installer banner keeps Mizobata's and Kon's credit lines unaltered and
adds one line for the update; the version reads "1.62-2026.1" so that the
1.62 number remains the author's.

modernized/plinkc/reference/ holds plinkc.a62.asm and PLINKC.OBJ, the reference
the derivative is checked against. PLINKC.OBJ is an unmodified copy of the
1999 object. plinkc.a62.asm is the author's source with two mechanical changes,
so that xasm2026-4 can assemble it: CR line endings turned into LF, and one
closing brace "}" added to a loop block that A62 tolerated open. It emits no
byte: the source still assembles to the 1999 PLINKC.OBJ byte for byte. The
unmodified source remains in original/PLINKC-1.62-1999/PLINKC.asm.


